        "\n",
        "The program uses a school management system to demonstrate inheritance.\n",
        "\n",
        "Person: This is the base class. It contains the common attributes name and age, which are shared by students and teachers.\n",
        "Student: This is a derived class that inherits from Person. It also contains student_id and course.\n",
        "Teacher: This class inherits from Person and has an additional attribute called subject.\n",
        "super().__init__(name, age): This calls the constructor of the parent class, allowing the derived classes to reuse the common attributes.\n",
        "\n",
        "Inheritance reduces code repetition because the student and teacher classes do not need to define their own copies of the common attributes"
