        "Explanation of encapsulation\n",
        "\n",
        "Encapsulation involves keeping certain data inside a class and controlling how it is accessed or modified.\n",
        "\n",
        "In this program:\n",
        "\n",
        "self.__student_id defines a name-mangled private attribute.\n",
        "get_student_id() retrieves the student's ID.\n",
        "set_student_id() allows the ID to be updated after checking that the new value is not empty.\n",
        "\n",
        "This helps prevent direct access to the attribute through its ordinary public name and provides a controlled way of updating it.\n",
        "\n",
        "Explanation of polymorphism\n",
        "\n",
        "Polymorphism allows the same method to produce different results depending on the object using it.\n",
        "\n",
        "In this example, both Student and Teacher have an introduce() method.\n",
        "\n",
        "For a student, the method returns the student's name and course.\n",
        "For a teacher, the method returns the teacher's name and subject.\n",
        "\n",
        "Although the method has the same name, its behaviour depends on the class of the object"
      ],
